WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.469
When we laugh, our brains 
release a cocktail&nbsp;of hormones.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.408
So we release endorphins,

00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:07.750
giving us a similar feeling 
to a runner’s high;

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:08.980
we&nbsp;lower our cortisol,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.944
making us feel calmer;

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:14.184
and we release dopamine, the same
 hormone released during&nbsp;sex,

00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:15.797
making us feel more bonded.

00:00:15.797 --> 00:00:19.294
So in essence, as far as our 
brains are concerned,

00:00:19.294 --> 00:00:20.934
laughing&nbsp;is like exercising,

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:21.704
meditating

00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:22.740
and having sex

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.885
at the same time.

00:00:24.885 --> 00:00:27.517
Laughing together makes us
 feel&nbsp;more connected.

00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:31.200
It floods our brains with the same 
hormones associated with love.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.500
And who doesn't&nbsp;want to feel more joy

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.015
and love in our lives?

00:00:35.015 --> 00:00:36.855
Where humor exists,

00:00:36.855 --> 00:00:38.830
love is not far behind.

